From 654c31a84b2ae2dfc33dfa80f7d45b10f594a973 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:52:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/18] ntsync: let ntsync win over esync, and keep objects
 alive while in use.

The GE-Proton 11.0-5 ntsync build hung at a black desktop with esync on
(Winlator's default): wineserver started esync and told clients so, but
the object code still picked ntsync. The proton-cachyos 11 series fixed
that and a lifetime bug; its ntsync patches produce the same
server/inproc_sync.c, esync and ntdll sync code on this tree, so they
replace the ones here:

- wineserver only turns esync on when ntsync is not usable, and clients
  follow wineserver's choice instead of reading WINEESYNC themselves;
  PROTON_NO_NTSYNC=1 brings esync back.
- closing the last handle to an object while another thread waits on it
  no longer fails the wait, and abandoned mutexes are reported: the
  reply carries a handle that keeps the object alive in the client.

The build fails if any of these did not land.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019oF8nnfMD8z5Z1MeNXoYS9
